          "content": {
            "id": "349c05c8-d178-3b40-8a38-22a7adb4f076",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Rare Earth Stocks Revive After China Slams Trump's Venezuela Intervention",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Rare earth stocks moved higher Monday after Beijing's denunciation of President Trump's intervention in Venezuela underscored the urgency of setting up a non-China supply chain for rare earth magnets critical for the U.S. military.  MP Materials, USA Rare Earth, American Resources, NioCorp Developments were among stocks to post gains.  Until Friday, the once red-hot rare-earth sector turned ice cold over the past few months, particularly after President Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping agreed to meet in South Korea in October, and reached some accommodation over rare-earth access.",
